Patch over libdmusic 790662e71120ff70359033083eb5a8a5751d5300 (MIT, https://github.com/frabert/libdmusic)
applied by scripts/build-dmrender.sh before building. What it changes and why:

- Common.h littleEndianRead: cast each byte to the target type before shifting; the int-promoted
  shift is undefined beyond bit 31, so every 64-bit field (GUID Data4, reference times) read garbage.
- Region/Instrument/Articulator: also accept the DLS Level 2 chunk ids (rgn2/lar2/art2). The
  Cultures banks are DLS2 files whose region and articulator payloads use the DLS1 layouts.
- Forms/Tracks.cpp: instantiate SequenceTrack for 'seqt' chunks; the class existed but the track
  factory never created it, so sequence-track notes were silently dropped.
- PlayingContext prepareSegment: schedule DX8 pattern tracks (DMPT) and sequence tracks (seqt) as
  absolute-time note messages. Every pattern track of a segment plays its embedded pattern
  simultaneously, looping until the segment header's mtLength (evidence: segments carry several
  DMPT tracks in one group with identical groove ranges, and the 30-measure patterns fit the
  30-measure segments exactly once). The upstream path pushed patterns into a groove-driven picker
  that nothing triggers in segments without a command track, so no notes ever played.
- PlayingContext loadBandTrack: clamp negative physical band times to 0. Cultures band items carry
  -1 ("apply before start"); as unsigned that landed at the end of the message queue and no
  instruments were ever loaded.
- MusicMessages BandChangeMessage: priority above notes, so instrument setup precedes notes that
  share its timestamp.
- MusicMessages getOffsetFromScale: a degree beyond the chord's note count projects into the next
  octave (the 4th tone of a triad is the root an octave up) instead of dropping the note; half the
  Cultures notes resolve chord tone 3 against the default triad.
- MusicMessages scheduleDx8PatternTrack/scheduleSequenceTrack: the schedulers the DMPT/seqt
  branches above use. Approximations: the default C chord (no segment carries a chord track),
  sequential variation choice per pattern repeat.
- dmrender: renderBlock counts interleaved samples, so size the buffer by channels and write
  length/channels wav frames; stereo renders wrote half music, half out-of-bounds reads. The
  buffer is zero-initialised so silent stretches are silence, not heap garbage.

